WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.300
Speaker 1: So there's a new report out that,
while shocking, shouldn't be hugely surprising

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.630
to anybody who's been paying attention for
the last six years.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:14.990
In a new book by Wall Street Journal reporter
Michael Bender, Bender writes that Donald

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:23.500
Trump told his then chief of staff, John Kelly,
in 2018 that Hitler, yes, Adolf Hitler did

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.500
a lot of good things.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.380
Now, remember that The Wall Street Journal
is owned by News Corp.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.560
That's the same company that owns Fox News.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.309
This is not some left wing publication or
left wing reporter.

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:39.680
The story goes that this took place during
a visit to Europe for the 100th anniversary

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.920
of the end of World War One.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.379
Now, you might I actually remember this was
one of the many disastrous trips that Trump

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.379
took.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.460
And I believe this was the one where he ended
up not going somewhere and they claimed it

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.640
was because of fog.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.880
But he just wanted to hang around and watch
Fox News.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.750
There was like some Leeth ring wreath laying
ceremony, something like that.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.750
I believe that's the same trip here.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.699
And during that trip, Donald Trump insisted
to John Kelly, who at the time was his chief

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:08.369
of staff, that, well, Hitler did a lot of
good things.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:12.090
The comments reportedly stunned John Kelly.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:17.329
This is all in a book that's hilariously titled,
frankly, we did win this election.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:21.609
You know, that's that's Trump, the guy, of
course, who is saying that.

00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:23.130
Speaker 2: Congratulations, sir.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.549
You just won the election.

00:01:24.549 --> 00:01:25.549
Yeah.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.599
Speaker 1: Now, the comment itself is outrageous
and stunning.

00:01:27.599 --> 00:01:34.049
There are rumors that Trump used to keep a
copy of Hitler's speeches on his bedside table.

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:35.049
Trump doesn't read.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:37.020
That's the one thing that makes me doubt that.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.530
But it's certainly possible.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.179
But the context here is actually even more
interesting.

00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:46.549
Trump apparently blurted this out during the
trip when John Kelly started explaining basic

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:47.639
history to Trump.

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:52.659
I guess, as was frequently done before an
event, people around Trump would try to give

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:56.549
him a little information about how the world
works so that he would maybe be able to avoid

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.369
humiliating himself.

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:02.829
And in so doing, John Kelly reminded Trump,
what were the different countries on each

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:04.819
side of World War One?

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:08.619
And then Kelly explained how World War One
connected to World War Two and of course,

00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:11.120
the Holocaust and the atrocities of Adolf
Hitler.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.070
And in that context, Trump's contribution,
Trump's interjection was, well, Hitler did

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.280
a lot of good things to an American president.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.400
Fox reportedly saying this.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.599
Now, of course, Trump's new spokeswoman, Liz
Harington, says it's all made up.

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:31.670
She says, quote, This is totally false.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.900
President Trump never said this.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:41.030
It is made up fake news probably by a general
who was incompetent and was fired.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:46.480
However, Bender seems to have done his job
and his homework and has multiple sources

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.480
on this.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:53.120
And in fact, multiple people told Bender everybody
in the room was saying to Trump, no, no, no,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.799
no, no, Hitler didn't do great things.

00:02:55.799 --> 00:03:00.439
And they were clearly horrified that Trump
might say that publicly at some point.

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:05.209
And Trump reportedly insisted, according to
multiple sources, no, Hitler did do great

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:10.280
things like, for example, leading the German
economic recovery in the nineteen thirties.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:16.359
Now, even that shows Trump's complete ignorance
and his deference to authoritarian and in

00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:19.599
some cases genocidal leaders.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:25.459
Trump seems to have no idea that the so-called
German economic revival was hugely based on

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:30.830
wealth that they stole from the people that
they eventually murdered.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:36.609
What I would have given to have been a fly
on the wall during this conversation and Bender

00:03:36.609 --> 00:03:43.170
ads in the book that Kelly told Trump, even
if your claim about the German economy under

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:48.709
the Nazis was true, like even if it were true
that Hitler did great things economically,

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:53.129
quote, you cannot ever say anything supportive
of Adolf Hitler.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:54.549
You just can't.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:04:00.269
And Kelly clearly realized that if he didn't
explain that to Trump, next thing you know,

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:02.090
Trump might be praising Hitler in public.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:08.219
And the book more generally outlines how clueless
Trump was about every aspect of history.

00:04:08.219 --> 00:04:15.620
Quote, Senior officials described his understanding
of slavery, Jim Crow or the black experience

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.840
in general post civil war as vague to nonexistent.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:25.050
But Trump's indifference to black history
was similar to his disregard for the history

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:29.110
of any race, religion or creed.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.270
It's actually crazy, but this sounds like
the type of things some Trump supporters would

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.590
actually say in defending Trump.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:41.830
Like when you confront a Trump supporter and
you say, listen, Trump is really authoritarian.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:47.360
His tendencies are like Duterte and they're
like Kim Jong un and they're like Putin.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.650
And, you know, some aspects are even Hitlerian
in some way.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:52.680
OK, man.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.050
But Hitler did some good things.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.890
I mean, the economy did well in the trains,
ran on time or whatever.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:03.729
It sounds exactly like the prototypical Trump
supporter, and I don't typically read these

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:07.789
types of books, I didn't read Fire and Fury,
I didn't read, you know, all of these different

00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:08.789
ones.

00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:10.669
Frankly, we did win this election.

00:05:10.669 --> 00:05:14.389
Sounds like one I may actually want to look
at, but certainly nothing.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:20.090
It's shocking, but it's not a surprise if
you've been following Donald Trump for as

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:24.230
long as anybody who's been following American
politics has been doing it.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:56.310
And curious to see if Trump will say anything
about it himself.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:30.009
Hey, you know,

